{"path":"numeric/valarray/tan","title":"std::tan(std::valarray)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>tan<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(std::valarray)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/tan","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"For each element in va computes tangent of the value of the element.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/valarray\">&lt;valarray&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> tan<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> va <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>For each element in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">va</span></code> computes tangent of the value of the element. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> va\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> value array to apply the operation to\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Value array containing tangents of the values in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">va</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Unqualified function (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">tan</span></code>) is used to perform the computation. If such function is not available, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tan\"><span class=\"kw1343\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tan</span></span></a></span></code> is used due to <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a>.\n</p><p>The function can be implemented with the return type different from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span>. In this case, the replacement type has the following properties:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> All <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span> member functions of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span> are provided.\n</li><li> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/slice_array\">std::slice_array</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/gslice_array\">std::gslice_array</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/mask_array\">std::mask_array</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/indirect_array\">std::indirect_array</a></span> can be constructed from the replacement type.\n</li><li> For every function taking a <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx11\"><span>except <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/begin2\"><code>begin()</code></a> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/end2\"><code>end()</code></a></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></span></span>, identical functions taking the replacement types shall be added;\n</li><li> For every function taking two <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> arguments, identical functions taking every combination of <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> and replacement types shall be added.\n</li><li> The return type does not add more than two levels of template nesting over the most deeply-nested argument type.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<table class=\"eq-fun-cpp-table\">\n<tr>\n<td>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\nvalarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> tan<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> va<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> other <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> va<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> i <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> other<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> tan<span class=\"br0\">(</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> other<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// proxy object may be returned</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;valarray&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> show <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> title, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> va<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> title <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"&nbsp;:\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> x <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> va<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"  \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1801\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fixed</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> x<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> x <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu18\">.0</span>, <span class=\"nu18\">.1</span>, <span class=\"nu18\">.2</span>, <span class=\"nu18\">.3</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> y <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tan\"><span class=\"kw1343\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tan</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan\"><span class=\"kw1346\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atan</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>y<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    show<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"x          \"</span>, x<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    show<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"y = tan(x) \"</span>, y<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    show<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"z = atan(y)\"</span>, z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>x          &nbsp;:  0.000000  0.100000  0.200000  0.300000\ny = tan(x) &nbsp;:  0.000000  0.100335  0.202710  0.309336\nz = atan(y)&nbsp;:  0.000000  0.100000  0.200000  0.300000</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/sin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sin<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sin\">std::sin</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/cos\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>cos<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/cos\">std::cos</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/atan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atan<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan\">std::atan</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>tan</span><span>tanf</span><span>tanl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes tangent (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\tan{x}}\">tan(x)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/tan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>tan<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes tangent of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\tan{z}}\">tan(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/valarray","title":"std::valarray"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::tan(std::valarray)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. For each element in va computes tangent of the value of the element."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"va"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Value array containing tangents of the values in va."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Unqualified function (tan) is used to perform the computation. If such function is not available, std::tan is used due to argument-dependent lookup."},{"label":"Possible implementation"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"sin(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::sin to each element of valarray"},{"label":"cos(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::cos to each element of valarray"},{"label":"atan(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::atan to each element of valarray"},{"label":"tan, tanf, tanl","note":"computes tangent (tan(x))"},{"label":"tan(std::complex)","note":"computes tangent of a complex number (tan(z))"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":355,"codeBlockCount":3}
